# numfmt_only_series.xlsx -- FROZEN EXPECTATION.
# A frozen expectation is corrected ONLY when the reading of the third-party-authored fixture was
# wrong -- never edited to chase an FSA1 regression.
#
# The `region:` lines are the SEMANTIC reading, written from the authored structure before `unpack`
# was run on this file. The `block:` lines are the hand-derivation below, executed on the fixture's
# own `s=` attributes.
#
# THE SIGNATURES, off xl/worksheets/sheet1.xml:
#   no s= at all on A1:B3    the preamble, General-formatted   -- None, the value an unstated
#                                                                 coordinate also carries
#   s="1" on A4:A11          the date column, yyyy-mm-dd       -- d
#   s="2" on B4:B11          the count column, #,##0           -- n
# xl/styles.xml states one font, one fill and one border -- the defaults -- and nothing else. The only
# thing separating the preamble from the series is the number format each xf carries, so this fixture
# splits at all only because `numFmtId` sits inside the signature. Read the look alone and all 22
# cells state the same nothing: the seed covers them as one 2x11 rectangle, and no cut then exists to
# make.
#
# 1. SEED. The None group is {A1,B1,A2,B2,A3,B3}: two wide, three deep -> A1:B3. d -> A4:A11. n ->
#    B4:B11. A rectangle of nothing but unstated coordinates costs no rule at all, so A1:B3 costs 0
#    and the two series columns cost 1 each: the potential is 2 + 3 lambda = 5.
#
# 2. PASS 1, parity 0: A1:B3 and B4:B11.
#    A1:B3 down takes A4:B4 across both its columns, cutting BOTH series columns to A5:A11 and
#    B5:B11. The merged A1:B4 has no modal -- three all-None rows and then a row of two signatures --
#    and neither column is uniform, so its two stated cells are leftovers: 2 rules. Before 0+1+1+1+
#    1+1 = 5, after 2+1 plus 1+1 and 1+1 = 7 -> -2. Columns C..E hold nothing, so it reaches nothing
#    sideways.
#    B4:B11 up takes B3, its own one column, cutting the preamble into A1:B2 and A3. Merged B3:B11 has
#    an unstated cell at its head, so there is no modal and each of its eight counts costs a rule: 8.
#    Before 1+1+0+1 = 3, after 8+1 plus 0+1 and 0+1 = 11 -> -8. Left it takes A4:A11 whole: the merged
#    A4:B11 is gapless, the dates are modal (a tie at eight cells each, broken to the first in
#    row-major order) and the count column is ONE column rule -> 2 rules. Before 1+1+1+1 = 4, after
#    2+1 = 3 -> +1, and it is applied. Regions: A1:B3, A4:B11.
#
# 3. PASS 2, parity 1: neither anchor is of that parity, so the pass is silent.
#
# 4. PASS 3, parity 0: both anchors again.
#    A1:B3 down takes A4:B4 and cuts the series to A5:B11: before 0+1+2+1 = 4, after rules(A1:B4) = 2,
#    +1, plus 2+1 = 6 -> -2.
#    A4:B11 up takes A3:B3 across both columns and cuts the preamble to A1:B2. The merged A3:B11 has
#    an unstated row at its head, so there is no modal; no column is uniform and no series row is
#    uniform either -- each row states a date beside a count -- so all sixteen series cells are
#    leftovers: 16 rules. Before 2+1+0+1 = 4, after 16+1 plus 0+1 = 18 -> -14.
#    Nothing applied, and the pass after it is the second silent one. TWO blocks, split exactly where
#    the series begins.
#
# 5. `--decompose occupancy` reads no signature: 22 occupied cells in a 2x11 bounding box, area 22,
#    under the policy's 256-cell floor, so it writes ONE block A1:B11. Of the two labelled starts --
#    rows 1 and 4 -- it emits row 1 and misses one.
sheet:  Series
region: 1-3 the metadata preamble
region: 4-11 the dated series, its date column and its count column
block:  A1:B3
block:  A4:B11
policy: appearance
misses: 1
